## Language

Always reply in 繁體中文, including after a long session or a compaction, and when relaying a subagent's English report. Code, identifiers and technical terms stay in their original form.

## Code search

Route by what the question asks for:

| Ask | Tool |
|---|---|
| **Intent** — where is X implemented, how does Y work, code like this spot | `mcp__semble__search` (`content`: `docs`\|`config`\|`all` beyond code; `repo`: the project root); from a hit, `mcp__semble__find_related` |
| **Literal** — every occurrence of a string or regex, all callers of a symbol, an exact message | `rg` (the Grep tool is ripgrep). Large repo (the search-tools plugin runs `tgrep serve` for it): `tgrep` from `<root>` with the same flags |
| **Shape** — a construct with variable parts (`foo($$$ARGS)`), a mechanical rewrite across files, a file's symbol outline | `ast-grep run -p '<pattern>' -l <lang>`; `-r '<fix>'` shows a diff, `-U` applies it; `ast-grep outline <path>` |

One search per question: land on the top intent hit and read there; the exhaustive list is for literal asks. From Bash, a tree search is `rg -n <pattern> [path]` (`grep -r` and `xargs grep` are refused by the plugin and cost a retry).

Before the first `tgrep` or `ast-grep` call in a session, load the `search-tools:reference` skill.

## File references

Write every file or directory you mention in a reply (a worktree too) as a markdown link to its absolute `file://` URL, with the repo-relative path (and `:line` when it points at a line) as the text: [src/app.ts:42](file:///home/me/repo/src/app.ts). The terminal turns it into a clickable OSC 8 link; a bare path is not clickable. Forward slashes, spaces as `%20`{{ if eq .chezmoi.os "windows" }}, drive letter after the third slash (`file:///C:/Users/...`){{ end }}. Code blocks and commands keep plain paths.

A web address gets the same shape, with a short name as the text, never a bare URL. Every pull request, merge request, issue, pipeline or commit you mention is such a link, named by its short form: [herdr#4748](https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr/issues/4748), [CRM!2612](https://git.gss.com.tw/CRM/CRM/-/merge_requests/2612); a bare `#4748` or `!2612` is not clickable.

## Dotfiles

chezmoi manages `~/.claude`, `~/.gitconfig` and the shared `~/.config` entries; `chezmoi managed` lists them, `~/.local/share/chezmoi/README.md` maps the source. Change a target only through its source (`chezmoi edit <target>`, then `chezmoi apply`): a drifted target makes `chezmoi apply` stop on an interactive prompt and hang the shell. In `settings.json`, only the keys listed in `.chezmoidata/claude.toml` come from the source; every other key stays local.

When `chezmoi status` shows drift, run `chezmoi diff <target>`, then `chezmoi apply --force <target>`. An `R` line is a script that runs on every apply, not drift.

## Tools

- Package manager: pnpm, unless the project's own lockfile names another. A global CLI from the npm registry installs with `pnpm add -g`.
- Wire an external tool in as its CLI plus a skill, not an MCP server: the CLI goes in `.chezmoidata/tools.toml`, the skill in `.chezmoidata/skills.toml`. An MCP server is for a tool that must stay resident (semble's index); it goes in `[claude.mcp]` of `.chezmoidata/claude.toml`.
- `!` commands get no stdin: a login that asks to paste a key or answer a prompt goes in a separate terminal window.
- Wait on a long job by starting it with `run_in_background` and acting on its completion notice.
{{- if ne .chezmoi.os "windows" }}
- The shell is zsh with `noclobber`: overwrite an existing file with `>|`, since a plain `>` onto it fails with "file exists".
- Stop processes by PID: `pgrep -f <pattern>`, check the list, then `kill <pid>`. `pkill -f` also matches the shell running it whenever the pattern sits in that shell's own command line, and kills it; a `pgrep -f` wait loop matches itself the same way and never ends.
{{- end }}
{{- if eq .chezmoi.os "windows" }}

## Windows shell

- `!` commands and the Bash tool run Git Bash: give the user `!` commands with forward slashes and no PowerShell cmdlets.
- Before a Bash command that passes a path, a file or another program's output between Git Bash, Node and pwsh, read `~/.claude/docs/windows-shell.md`: path rewriting, two `/tmp` folders, `\r` line ends, console encoding, pwsh arguments.
{{- end }}
